   "t": "Mrs Iyer, Dev, you're in room three. The doctor's ready. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Thank you. Come, Dev. Doctor, we're back about the nosebleeds."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Hello Dev, hello Mrs Iyer. Last time, we tried the cream and the pinching. How has it gone? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "A little better, doctor. But he still gets them, two or three a week, mostly in the morning."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How long does each one last?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Long. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Ten minutes, sometimes more, doctor. He holds a tissue and it keeps coming."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Dev, do you pick your nose?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Sometimes. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "He does. I tell him, but he forgets."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Is the cream helping? You're putting it on every day?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Twice a day, the nasal cream. We've used it for two weeks."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any bruising on his body that you've noticed, or bleeding gums?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "No, nothing like that. His gums are fine. No bruises beyond the football."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any family history of bleeding problems? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "No. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Hay fever, perhaps?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Yes, he has hay fever, every summer. He rubs his nose a lot."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That fits. I'll check him over. Temperature and pulse, please. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_4",
   "t": "I'll do those, doctor. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_4",
   "t": "Temperature 36.7, pulse 88, blood pressure 102 over 64, oxygen 99 percent, respiratory rate 20."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you, Priya. Now Dev, can I look up your nose with a light? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Both sides are red and crusty at the front, and there's one tiny blood vessel on the right that's easy to bleed. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "What does that mean? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It's the usual place for these. It's not serious, but it's persistent, so I'd like to look further. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "What will you do? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to check a blood count and a clotting screen, to make sure his blood clots normally."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Will it hurt him? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "A quick prick in the arm, and it's done. Priya will take him through. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_4",
   "t": "I'll take care of him, Mrs Iyer. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Keep the cream going, twice a day, and keep his nails short. A little petroleum jelly inside the nose at night helps keep it moist."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "We'll do that. And if it bleeds? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Sit up, lean forward, pinch the soft part for ten minutes without letting go. If it lasts more than twenty minutes, or he's pale or drowsy, come in straight away."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Understood. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And if the blood tests show anything unusual, we'll call you in."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Thank you, doctor. ~"
  }
